Regarding weapon damage, I think Grawyswandir + silver sabre is
considered the best combination.  Grayswandir does double damage to
everything, plus d20 extra to the silver haters (the d20 isn't
doubled...).  Frost Brand only does double damage to non-cold
resistant monsters.  Long swords do d12 against large monsters, sabres
do d8 (both do d8 against small creatures) which is 2 more points
damage on average for FB.  I'll happily trade +2 damage doubled
against most monsters for double damage against all +d20 against some.

Also, your analysis can get more complicated... only archaeologists
can get to expert in sabre, but they can only get basic in twoweapon
and long sword (and that only after being gifted with a long sword
artifact).  OTOH, a knight, for instance, can get to skilled in sabre
and twoweapon and expert in long sword.

In short, it's pretty close to a toss up unless you are considering
silver hating monsters.  Then, Grayswandir/sabre combo is the winner
hands down!

